# [[.Name]]

A project CLI powered by Loop's shared runtime.

## Develop

The generated command is an example GET `/health`. Adapt `project.json` and the
fixture in `contracts_test.go` and `main_test.go` to the actual admin API before distributing it.

```sh
go mod tidy
go test ./...
go run . describe
go build -o bin/[[.Name]] .
```

Go 1.26 or later is needed for development. Installed executables need no Go runtime.
Commit `go.sum` after resolving the pinned SDK. The initial module path is
`loop.local/[[.Name]]`; it can be changed to your repository's module path if needed.
The scaffold template version and SDK pin are recorded in `.loop/scaffold.json`.
Use this directory as the CLI repository root. Initialisation does not create a Git
repository or remote. If the CLI belongs inside a larger repository, integrate its
workflows at that repository's `.github/workflows/` and adjust working directories
before expecting GitHub Actions to run them.

With Loop installed, `loop run --manifest project.json -- describe` works without
Go or API credentials. The built CLI embeds the same `project.json`.

## Connect to the project

Set `[[.BaseURLEnv]]` to the admin API base URL and `[[.TokenEnv]]` to an authorised
bearer token using your existing credential setup. Then run:

```sh
go run . status get
```

Help and `describe` do not require credentials. Results go to stdout, structured
errors to stderr. Tests use their own local fixture and never contact the real API.
On Windows, build to `bin/[[.Name]].exe` and run `.\bin\[[.Name]].exe`.

## Release

The included CI runs on Linux, macOS and Windows, each on amd64 and arm64. After
successful verification, pushing a `v*` tag triggers GoReleaser to publish archives
and SHA-256 checksums to this repository's GitHub Releases. No extra release token
is needed for that default recipe. Repository Actions policies still apply.

Read the [release skill](.agents/skills/[[.Name]]-release/SKILL.md) before choosing a
distribution destination. Reuse suitable organisation infrastructure and configured
registries before creating a new tap, bucket or registry. No external setup or
publication happens during `loop init`.

Once this directory is committed in a Git repository with its intended remote,
run `goreleaser check`, then
`goreleaser release --snapshot --clean --skip=publish,sign` using the workflow's
pinned GoReleaser version. For installation from a release, download the archive
matching the OS/architecture, verify its checksum, and put the executable on PATH.
Package-manager setup and platform signing are configured for the chosen publisher.
